{"search_note":"I found good evidence on program design, budget allocation, and some beneficiary counts, but much less independent evidence on actual distributional outcomes by caste, region, and class in 2024.

The strongest positive evidence is often official self-reporting or scheme statistics; the strongest negative evidence is from Reuters on coalition-state favoritism and persistent rural distress.

There is little direct evidence that Modi systematically equalized gains across all regions and social groups; the record looks uneven.","evidence":[{"title":"India's finance minister unveils budget with focus on poor, women, youth and farmers","publisher":"Reuters via ThePrint","date":"2024-02-01","url":"https://theprint.in/india/indias-finance-minister-unveils-budget-with-focus-on-poor-women-youth-and-farmers/1948406/","summary":"The interim budget explicitly prioritized the poor, women, youth, and farmers, and was framed as fiscally restrained rather than a giveaway budget. This is positive evidence for broad distribution, not just elite or supporter-only favors.","question_ids":["5B.8","5B.1","5B.6","5B.7"]},{"title":"With handouts, piped water and cooking gas, India's Modi woos women voters","publisher":"Reuters via ThePrint","date":"2024-02-28","url":"https://theprint.in/india/with-handouts-piped-water-and-cooking-gas-indias-modi-woos-women-voters/1981512/","summary":"Reuters found many women in Modi-leaning regions crediting BJP policies such as piped water, electricity, cooking gas, and cash benefits. This is evidence that economic gains were reaching at least some women and poor households, though the article also shows these benefits were electorally salient.","question_ids":["5B.8","5B.6","5B.7"]},{"title":"Women empowerment remained in focus for rural development ministry in 2024","publisher":"PTI via ThePrint","date":"2024-12-31","url":"https://theprint.in/india/women-empowerment-remained-in-focus-for-rural-development-ministry-in-2024/2425889/","summary":"The rural development ministry said women were central to its 2024 schemes, with over half of MGNREGS beneficiaries women and PMAY-G housing strongly favoring women ownership. This is strong positive evidence for gender-targeted distribution.","question_ids":["5B.8","5B.6"]},{"title":"Cabinet approves implementation of the Pradhan Mantri Awaas Yojana - Gramin (PMAY-G) during FY 2024-25 to 2028-29","publisher":"Press Information Bureau / Ministry of Rural Development","date":"2024-08-09","url":"https://www.pib.gov.in/Pressreleaseshare.aspx?PRID=2043919&lang=2&reg=48","summary":"The Cabinet extended PMAY-G with different unit assistance for hill and northeastern states, which is a real attempt at regional differentiation rather than a one-size-fits-all model.","question_ids":["5B.8","5B.6"]},{"title":"PMAY-G enabling convergence of schemes, aim to link women beneficiaries with NRLM: Official","publisher":"PTI via ThePrint","date":"2024-11-20","url":"https://theprint.in/india/pmay-g-enabling-convergence-of-schemes-aim-to-link-women-beneficiaries-with-nrlm-official/2365891/","summary":"PMAY-G houses were being sanctioned in women’s names or joint ownership, and officials said the scheme was being used to link women beneficiaries to livelihood programs. This supports a fairer gender distribution of asset ownership.","question_ids":["5B.8","5B.6"]},{"title":"Details of the total number of women who have benefited from the Lakhpati Didi and Namo Didi initiatives, State-wise and category-wise","publisher":"Press Information Bureau / Ministry of Rural Development","date":"2024-12-03","url":"https://www.pib.gov.in/Pressreleaseshare.aspx?PRID=2080093&lang=2&reg=48","summary":"The government reported 10.05 crore rural households mobilized into SHGs and state/category-wise participation including SC/ST/OBC groups. This is positive evidence of spread across class/caste lines, though it is official self-reporting.","question_ids":["5B.8","5B.6"]},{"title":"Deendayal Antyodaya Yojana -NRLM Mission Mobilises more than 10 Crore Women from Rural Households into 90.86 Lakh SHGs","publisher":"Press Information Bureau / Ministry of Rural Development","date":"2024-07-30","url":"https://www.pib.gov.in/PressReleaseIframePage.aspx?PRID=2039162&lang=2&reg=48","summary":"DAY-NRLM had mobilized more than 10 crore women from rural households into SHGs across 28 states and 6 UTs. That is strong evidence of broad rural-gender distribution, especially for poorer households.","question_ids":["5B.8","5B.6"]},{"title":"India focuses on job creation, rural areas in first budget after election","publisher":"Reuters via ThePrint","date":"2024-07-23","url":"https://theprint.in/india/india-focuses-on-job-creation-rural-areas-in-first-budget-after-election/2186863/","summary":"The first post-election budget kept spending on jobs and rural programs high, alongside incentives for manufacturing and higher education loans. This is positive on distribution to workers and rural households, but it was also clearly reactive to political pressure.","question_ids":["5B.8","5B.1","5B.4","5B.6","5B.7"]},{"title":"Key allies of India's Modi demand nearly $6 billion for their states this year - document shows","publisher":"Reuters via ThePrint","date":"2024-07-05","url":"https://theprint.in/india/key-allies-of-indias-modi-demand-nearly-6-billion-for-their-states-this-year-document-shows/2162261/","summary":"Modi’s allies demanded large extra transfers for their home states, including infrastructure and medical college funding. This is counterevidence because it suggests region-specific bargaining tied to coalition support.","question_ids":["5B.8","5B.5","5B.6","5B.7"]},{"title":"India's Modi spends billions on jobs, key allies in first budget after election","publisher":"Reuters via ThePrint","date":"2024-07-23","url":"https://theprint.in/india/indias-modi-spends-billions-on-jobs-key-allies-in-first-budget-after-election/2187546/","summary":"Reuters said the budget devoted over $5 billion to two coalition-led states and was explicitly designed to win back voters and retain political support. This is the clearest evidence that gains were not distributed neutrally, but were skewed toward supporters and kingmaker regions.","question_ids":["5B.8","5B.1","5B.4","5B.5","5B.7"]},{"title":"India's Modi faces delicate balancing act in post-election budget","publisher":"Reuters via ThePrint","date":"2024-07-23","url":"https://theprint.in/india/indias-modi-faces-delicate-balancing-act-in-post-election-budget/2186495/","summary":"Reuters described the budget as balancing fiscal prudence with disgruntled voters and coalition demands, and noted complaints that it could “bribe” coalition partners and undermine other regions. This is strong counterevidence to fair, nonpartisan distribution.","question_ids":["5B.8","5B.1","5B.4","5B.5","5B.7"]},{"title":"Rural vote fall cost India's Modi a decisive election win","publisher":"Reuters via ThePrint","date":"2024-06-07","url":"https://theprint.in/india/rural-vote-fall-cost-indias-modi-a-decisive-election-win/2121496/","summary":"Reuters linked BJP losses in rural constituencies to lack of jobs and high inflation. That is counterevidence that gains were being shared fairly with lower-income and rural groups.","question_ids":["5B.8","5B.1","5B.7"]},{"title":"India's high food inflation leaves less in lunch boxes of poor school children","publisher":"Reuters via ThePrint","date":"2024-10-11","url":"https://theprint.in/india/indias-high-food-inflation-leaves-less-in-lunch-boxes-of-poor-school-children/2307077/","summary":"High food inflation squeezed school meal quality for poor children because budgets were not updated fast enough. This is direct counterevidence that the poorest groups were protected from macro pressures.","question_ids":["5B.8","5B.7"]},{"title":"India's finance minister unveils budget with focus on poor, women, youth and farmers","publisher":"Reuters via ThePrint","date":"2024-02-01","url":"https://theprint.in/india/indias-finance-minister-unveils-budget-with-focus-on-poor-women-youth-and-farmers/1948406/","summary":"Reuters noted that the government said the economy was in “profound transformation” and that the budget would focus on disadvantaged groups. This is a positive sign on paper, but it is still a government-led framing rather than independent proof of equal outcomes.","question_ids":["5B.8","5B.7"]}]}
